      "wrapperType": "software",
      "currency": "GBP",
      "description": "Safari on the iPhone Duo's outer display keeps its controls in a strip down the side, and web pages stop short of it. Sidefill gives that strip back to the page.\n\nEDGE TO EDGE\nPhone-width pages are laid out across the whole outer display, right under Safari's side controls. Articles, photos and video get the room the screen already has.\n\nSTILL TAPPABLE\nLinks, menus and buttons that would land under the controls move back into reach. Fixed headers and tab bars carry their colour to the edge while their contents stay clear. An optional blur keeps the controls readable over busy pages.\n\nONE SWITCH\nChoose Wide or Off from Safari's page menu. The choice applies to every site and tab, and any single site can be left as it is with one tap. Desktop-width pages are never touched; they look exactly as Safari shows them.\n\nPRIVATE BY DESIGN\nNo account, no analytics, no network requests. Sidefill adjusts layouts on your iPhone and never reads or sends what you browse.\n\nONE PURCHASE\nBuy it once and keep it. No subscription, no in-app purchases.\n\nSETUP\n1. Settings › Apps › Safari › Extensions › Sidefill\n2. Turn on Allow Extension and set All Websites to Allow\n3. In Safari, open the page menu › Sidefill › Wide\n\nSidefill is made for the iPhone Duo. On other iPhones Safari already uses the full width, so there is nothing for Sidefill to change.",
